{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0781419b7dbad767f9b8a73378e3abd74dd74f22d865fbb8284a76d9c5878171","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot cache janitor and materialization","key_entities":["docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md","src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","_gc_pass","materialize_tickets","add_bytes","byte_total","max_bytes","REBAR_GATE_MAX_BYTES","_is_entry","startup_sweep","cache.acquire","mtime"],"problem_keywords":["snapshot store","garbage collection","disk reclamation","byte accounting","cache eviction","size-based trigger","incremental counter"],"propositions":["The ADR-promised byte-total backstop trigger does not exist in _gc_pass; it reads only free disk space and entry mtime, never consulting the incremental byte_total counter.","materialize_tickets bypasses cache.acquire and populates entries without calling add_bytes, leaving ~620 MiB entries unaccounted in the store's incremental total.","The snapshot store has no size-based reclaim trigger at all because the backstop does not exist and the dominant entry kind (tickets-<sha>) contributes zero bytes to the accounting.","A configurable max_bytes cap with LRU eviction under a grace window is needed to implement the ADR 0005 D5 promise and restore store-size accountability."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787269545809635827,"uuid":"14e3f700-c736-4c34-b8df-1722b92ff406"}